<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5254" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμηχαν-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>want
				of means</i> or <i>resources, helplessness,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμηχανίη δ᾽ ἔχε θυμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.295
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πενίην μητέρ᾽ ἀμηχανίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					385
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				619
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				92
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.111
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ᾽ ἀμηχανίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					475
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<i>hardship, trouble,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειμῶνος ἀμηχανίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					496
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
